/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:18:| `P01_PCD` | Labelled strict posets.  Put `x<y` in the next order exactly when the old principal ideal of `x` is smaller than that of `y` and the old principal filter of `x` is larger than that of `y`. | All 4,231 labelled posets through `n=5`; extensive, only fixed recurrence, maximum tail first reaches 2 and maximum fibre 25. | **KILL_CURRENT.** The monotone signal is real, but no sharp all-rank clock or target-local inverse emerged; degree-pair realisation couples the fibre. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:21:| `G01_MMS` | Labelled simple graphs.  Retain precisely the edges belonging to at least one maximum matching. | Every graph through `n=5`; exact retraction, image 654 of 1,024 and maximum fibre 9 at `n=5`. | **KILL_MATCHING_CORE.** Allowed-edge support is a standard maximum-matching object and idempotence supplies no independent clock. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:24:| `G04_TTC` | Labelled simple graphs.  Retain an old edge exactly when its endpoints have identical closed neighbourhoods. | Through `n=5`; exact retraction, 52 fixed images and maximum fibre 588. | **KILL_TRUE_TWIN_INTERNAL.** True-twin quotient/projection machinery is already a permanent earlier control. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:25:| `G05_ECC` | Labelled simple graphs.  Inside each old connected component, join exactly pairs having equal old eccentricity. | Through `n=5`; exact retraction, 52 fixed images and maximum fibre 113. | **KILL_METRIC_RETRACTION.** Eccentricity classification and the one-step clock are the same statistic. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:26:| `T01_UTR` | Labelled tournaments.  Reverse simultaneously every arc contained in exactly one old directed triangle. | Every tournament through `n=6` (32,768 at the last rank); maximum tail 4, periods 1, 2, 4, image 17,168, maximum fibre 12. | **KILL_CURRENT / RAW LEAD ONLY.** The literal rule is lively, but the period strata are not classified, no fibre axis exists, and P112 already contains the closely adjacent “at least one directed triangle” reversal reserve. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:29:| `H02_PCP` | Labelled 3-uniform hypergraphs.  Retain an old triple iff each of its pairs has old codegree at least two. | Through `n=5`; maximum tail 2, image 182, fixed 52, maximum fibre 368. | **KILL_CODEGREE_CORE.** Pair-codegree pruning and core peeling are earlier permanent controls. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:30:| `H03_OCF` | Labelled 3-uniform hypergraphs.  Output a triple iff the sum of its three old pair-codegrees is odd. | Through `n=5`; at the last rank image=fixed=64 and maximum fibre 16. | **KILL_PARITY_COLLAPSE.** The state is compressed to a low-rank mod-two incidence statistic in one round. |
/root/autodl-tmp/symbolic_dynamics/docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/combinatorial_crossdomain/IDEA_LEDGER.md:35:| `Q02_CBF` | Permutations.  Build the min-Cartesian tree whose inorder word is the state, then output its labels in breadth-first order. | Every permutation through `S_9`; unique identity attractor, sharp maximum tail `n-1`, complete compatible-shape fibre formula, Catalan maximum. | **KILL_INTERNAL_CARTESIAN_TRAVERSAL.** P142's Cartesian-min preorder control already has the same carrier, prefix clock, Catalan extremum and tree-fibre engine; changing traversal does not clear the proof-transfer gate. |
